TI  - Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy for the diagnosis of lepidic-predominant lung 
      adenocarcinoma.
PG  - 434-437
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_325_18 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is one of the most common malignancies globally with lung 
      adenocarcinoma as the most common type of lung cancer. With new classification of 
      lung cancers in 2011, it has become pertinent that adequate tissue is obtained 
      for the diagnosis and subtyping of lung adenocarcinoma particularly for 
      prognostication. Transbronchial cryobiopsy is a minimally invasive procedure 
      which helps obtain adequate tissue and avoid surgical lung biopsy.
