TI  - Respiratory Bronchiolitis-associated Interstitial Lung Disease in a Nonsmoker 
      with Biomass Fuel Exposure.
PG  - 7-10
LID - 10.59556/japi.73.1237 [doi]
AB  - A 40-year-old nonsmoking female with a history of biomass fuel exposure presented 
      with a persistent dry cough and progressive dyspnea, ultimately diagnosed as 
      respiratory bronchiolitis-associated interstitial lung disease (RBILD) through 
      transbronchial cryobiopsy. This case highlights the rare occurrence of RBILD in 
      nonsmokers and emphasizes the diagnostic value of cryobiopsy in unexplained 
      interstitial lung disease. Multidisciplinary collaboration was essential for 
      accurate diagnosis and management.
